WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.240
Commissioning and handover connect design intent to an accepted operating system.

2
00:00:04.820 --> 00:00:09.640
Preserve the installed configuration and document revisions, the conditions tested, the acceptance

3
00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:11.400
results and any restrictions.

4
00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:15.900
Include the limits the operator must maintain at electrical and thermal handoffs.

5
00:00:16.580 --> 00:00:18.760
Identify monitoring and response ownership.

6
00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:22.800
The operator needs to know which signals matter, which actions are automatic,

7
00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:26.020
and which require an authorized procedure or another team.

8
00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:30.380
An exception accepted during deployment must remain visible after the project team

9
00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:30.800
leaves.

10
00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:33.340
Also define change triggers.

11
00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:38.740
Replacing equipment, changing fluid, rerouting hoses or updating a control revision can

12
00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:40.760
affect previously accepted interfaces.

13
00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:44.600
Not every change requires the same review, but none should be assumed

14
00:00:44.660 --> 00:00:47.140
harmless solely because the rack still powers on.

15
00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:52.700
A concise, traceable handover record supports operation, recovery and later integration.

16
00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:56.880
It is part of readiness, not an administrative step after readiness has

17
00:00:56.960 --> 00:00:57.880
already been declared.

